 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.5,
   "end": 5.269,
   "text": "The crowd was so big, he sat in a boat, and taught them from the water.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 5.669,
   "end": 7.799,
   "text": "A farmer went out to sow his seed.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 8.099,
   "end": 15.317,
   "text": "Some fell on the path, and birds ate it. Some on rock, and it withered. Some among thorns, and it was choked.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 15.716,
   "end": 21.181,
   "text": "But some fell on good soil. And it grew. Thirty, sixty, a hundred times.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 21.781,
   "end": 28.518,
   "text": "The kingdom of God is like a mustard seed. The smallest seed, that grows into the biggest tree.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 29.218,
   "end": 32.945,
   "text": "That evening he said: Let's go across to the other side.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 33.345,
   "end": 36.686,
   "text": "He lay down in the back of the boat, and fell asleep.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 37.486,
   "end": 42.861,
   "text": "Then a furious storm came. Waves broke over the boat. It was filling with water.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 43.061,
   "end": 44.818,
   "text": "Teacher! Don't you care if we drown?",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 45.318,
   "end": 46.579,
   "text": "Quiet. Be still.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 47.979,
   "end": 51.708,
   "text": "The wind died down. And it was completely calm.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 52.508,
   "end": 56.059,
   "text": "Why are you so afraid? Do you still have no faith?",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 56.859,
   "end": 63.116,
   "text": "They were terrified, and asked each other: Who is this? Even the wind and the waves obey him.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 64.016,
   "end": 67.317,
   "text": "Follow for part seven.",
   "tempter": false
  }
 ]
}